 "about": "Feature GPU cost budgets (plan 2.10's table, whole, and renderer pass 2's Stage A features at the plan's section 4 budgets, owner decision D17), Apple M4 Max, 1920x1080. A budget applies to a profile row when every feature it lists is switched on and wired for that row, in the shapes it names (applied.featureShapes) if any. A Stage A entry charges a feature's steady cost per frame (probe and volume shading, not their time-sliced captures and bakes). The stream entries (game systems STR-26b) are the frame thread's per-frame streaming budgets, not GPU features: `stream-finish-<class>` the view set's milliseconds of decoding and uploading (`budgetMs`, main-thread time), `stream-upload-<class>` and `stream-upload-web` the read bytes it uploads (`budgetBytes`; a browser takes the smaller of its class's row and the web cap). No profile row switches their features on, so they never charge a renderer feature's cost; the stream-valley fly-through rows read them and hold them equal to genex-render's `stream_budget`.",
